{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>Is it not enough that you lord it over us — also to lord it over us?</b> The Torah has inverted letters (in גם/כי), and it means: כי גם תשתרר עלינו השתרר — 'for also us you lord it over, to lord it over.' Example: וברכתם גם אותי — read: כי גם אותי, 'for also me.' Another interpretation: 'for you lord it over us' — you also <b>lord it over</b> Aaron your brother."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:18:14.233250572Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}